msgid "OpenID Connect (OIDC) and OAuth2 client and filters"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use Quarkus extensions for OpenID Connect and OAuth 2.0 access token "
"management, focusing on acquiring, refreshing, and propagating tokens."
msgstr ""

msgid "This includes the following:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using `quarkus-oidc-client`, `quarkus-rest-client-oidc-filter` and `quarkus-"
"resteasy-client-oidc-filter` extensions to acquire and refresh access tokens "
"from OpenID Connect and OAuth 2.0 compliant Authorization Servers such as "
"link:https://www.keycloak.org[Keycloak]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using `quarkus-rest-client-oidc-token-propagation` and `quarkus-resteasy-"
"client-oidc-token-propagation` extensions to propagate the current `Bearer` "
"or `Authorization Code Flow` access tokens."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The access tokens managed by these extensions can be used as HTTP "
"Authorization Bearer tokens to access the remote services."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Also see xref:security-openid-connect-client.adoc[OpenID Connect client and "
"token propagation quickstart]."
msgstr ""

msgid "OidcClient"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add the following dependency:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus-oidc-client` extension provides a reactive `io.quarkus.oidc."
"client.OidcClient`, which can be used to acquire and refresh tokens by using "
"SmallRye Mutiny `Uni` and `Vert.x WebClient`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`OidcClient` is initialized at build time with the IDP token endpoint URL, "
"which can be auto-discovered or manually configured.\n"
"`OidcClient` uses this endpoint to acquire access tokens with token grants "
"such as `client_credentials` or `password`, and to refresh tokens with a "
"`refresh_token` grant."
msgstr ""

msgid "Token endpoint configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the token endpoint address is discovered by adding a `/.well-"
"known/openid-configuration` path to the configured `quarkus.oidc-client.auth-"
"server-url`."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example, given this Keycloak URL:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`OidcClient` will discover that the token endpoint URL is `http://localhost:"
"8180/auth/realms/quarkus/protocol/openid-connect/tokens`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the OIDC provider requires authentication to access the discovery "
"endpoint, you can configure `OidcClient` to send credentials with the "
"discovery request, as described in <<oidc-client-authenticated-discovery-"
"endpoint>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the discovery endpoint is unavailable or you want to avoid an extra round-"
"trip to it, you can disable discovery and configure the token endpoint "
"address with a relative path."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

