"If you do not specify the `quarkus.oidc-client-graphql.client-name` "
"property, GraphQL clients will use the default OIDC client without an "
"explicit name."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specifically for type-safe GraphQL clients, you can override this on a per-"
"client basis by annotating the `GraphQLClientApi` interface with `@io."
"quarkus.oidc.client.filter.OidcClientFilter`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To use this with a programmatically created GraphQL client, both builders, "
"`VertxDynamicGraphQLClientBuilder` and `VertxTypesafeGraphQLClientBuilder`, "
"contain a `dynamicHeader(String, Uni<String>)` method that lets you plug in "
"a header that might change for every request."
msgstr ""

msgid "To plug an OIDC client into it, use:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For dynamic GraphQL clients, you can override the `quarkus.oidc-client-"
"graphql.client-name` configuration property on a per-client basis with the "
"`quarkus.oidc-client-graphql.\"graphql-client\".client-name` configuration "
"property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `dynamic-graphql-client-2` GraphQL client calls have the `Authorization` "
"header with an access token acquired by the `oidc-client-for-graphql-2` OIDC "
"client."
msgstr ""

